  "texts": {
    "preamble": "H.Hara Sabath vs State Of Ap on 27 August, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4936 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/A1 seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.154 of 2018 of Gopalapatnam Police Station, Visakhapatnam District, which was registered against him for the offence under Sections 188, 273 of IPC and Sec.59(i), 59(iii) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 17.06.2018 at 16.00 hours, when the complainant along with his staff visited Fish market, Gopalapatnam main road area, they found one unknown person with two luggage bags contain tobacco products, on that the Police stopped the person and on enquiry, he revealed that he has been transporting the tobacco products illegally to various places, the Police seized the same under the cover of mediator's report and registered the same as a case in Crime No.154 of 2018 for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "arguments": "",
